  "feature": "experimental-multihop-delegation",
  "$comment": "Opted-in counterpart of del-010 (#176 item 11). The input is del-010's, byte for byte: del-001's single-hop token plus a `jti` claim in the RFC-AITP-0005 §2.2 layout and no `chain`, minted by the runner as for del-010. A non-opted-in verifier rejects the same token with UNKNOWN_FIELD (del-010).",
  "description": "A verifier that HAS opted into RFC-AITP-0011 receives a single-hop delegation token carrying a well-formed `jti` and no `chain`. RFC-AITP-0011 §1.1: an opted-in implementation MUST accept an OPTIONAL `jti` on any delegation token. With no `chain`, the token is verified as a single-hop delegation under RFC-AITP-0006 and is accepted.",
